<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tatars</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tatar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tatars is a name applied to various Turkic-speaking peoples of the Eurasian steppe, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars">Crimean Tatars</a> who raided and fought along the borders of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> both fought against Tatar raiders and drew on Tatar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> traditions in developing its light cavalry. Accounts of the Commonwealth describe these frontier warrior cultures as an important military resource.</p></div>
